into a file named filename.txt. 
If everything works, the program will print "Successfully wrote to the file." in the console. 
If something goes wrong (for example, the file cannot be opened), it will print "An error occurred." instead.

Since Java 7, you can use try-with-resources. 
This makes sure the writer is closed automatically, even if an error occurs:

