code_examples.code:
Example
int num = 153;
int original = num;
int result = 0;
int digits = String.valueOf(num).length();

while (num != 0) {
 int digit = num % 10;
 result += Math.pow(digit, digits);
 num /= 10;
}

System.out.println(original + (result == original ? " is Armstrong" : " is not Armstrong"));
Try it Yourself »

Explanation: 
An Armstrong number means: take each digit, raise it to the power of the number of digits, and add them together. 

For 153 (3 digits): 

- First digit: 1&sup3 = 1 

- Second digit: 5&sup3 = 125 

- Third digit: 3&sup3 = 27 

Now add them: 1 + 125 + 27 = 153. 

Since the sum is the same as the original number, 153 is an Armstrong number.

